sparky-stereo-language-tasks (1.0.9+lc1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Retire Debian's own task packages (built from the tasksel source, each
    locked to tasksel's exact version) when the plan for tasksel would remove
    them, and keep what they brought: the installed packages they depend on
    or recommend are marked as installed by the person. A machine with
    task-laptop, task-english and a language task at tasksel 3.91 no longer
    holds tasksel back and no longer fails with "Remv: task-laptop".
  * Say what really failed: packages the plan would remove, a fetch that
    failed, or apt's own error; "check the network" only for a fetch. Two new
    messages in the ten languages.
  * A failed migration waits for a new request (the next package transaction)
    or the next boot. The service is no longer wanted by multi-user.target, so
    it never holds the boot; its path unit reacts to a change of the queue
    (PathChanged) instead of to the queue's existence, so a run that failed is
    not started again by its own path unit, and a timer starts it once, 30
    seconds after the manager starts, when work is queued.
  * Queue the migration when a Debian task holds tasksel back after an
    earlier migration finished.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0000

